********************************************  Step 1 — Create new readiness target group
aws elbv2 create-target-group ^
  --name tgrp-wnxt-int-user-readiness ^
  --protocol HTTP ^
  --port 80 ^
  --protocol-version HTTP1 ^
  --vpc-id vpc-4c677e2a ^
  --health-check-protocol HTTP ^
  --health-check-path "/readiness" ^
  --health-check-port "8080" ^
  --health-check-interval-seconds 20 ^
  --health-check-timeout-seconds 5 ^
  --healthy-threshold-count 2 ^
  --unhealthy-threshold-count 2 ^
  --matcher HttpCode=200 ^
  --target-type instance ^
  --region us-east-1
*************************************  Get the ARN
aws elbv2 describe-target-groups ^
  --names tgrp-wnxt-int-user-readiness ^
  --query "TargetGroups[*].TargetGroupArn" ^
  --region us-east-1
************************************* Update ALB rule to use readiness target group
aws elbv2 modify-rule ^
  --rule-arn arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:us-east-1:604009108246:listener-rule/app/alb-wnxt-i/e6fe1b87c2e6eede/3e4ac046072ca13a/60824d35dd9d96e1 ^
  --actions Type=forward,TargetGroupArn=arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:us-east-1:604009108246:targetgroup/tgrp-wnxt-int-user-readiness/f41e3007f3d1d40b ^
  --region us-east-1
************************************ Verify the rule was updated
aws elbv2 describe-rules ^
  --listener-arn arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:us-east-1:604009108246:listener/app/alb-wnxt-i/e6fe1b87c2e6eede/3e4ac046072ca13a ^
  --query "Rules[?Priority=='10'].{Priority:Priority,TG:Actions[0].TargetGroupArn,Condition:Conditions[0].Values}" ^
  --region us-east-1
*********************************** Step 4 — Attach readiness target group to ASG (So every new instance auto-registers in both target groups:)
aws autoscaling attach-load-balancer-target-groups ^
  --auto-scaling-group-name WNXT-INT-USER-ASG ^
  --target-group-arns arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:us-east-1:604009108246:targetgroup/tgrp-wnxt-user-readiness/c14ddc75fcc7d582 ^
  --region us-east-1
***********************************  Verify ASG has two Target Groups
aws autoscaling describe-auto-scaling-groups ^
  --auto-scaling-group-names WNXT-INT-USER-ASG ^
  --query "AutoScalingGroups[*].TargetGroupARNs" ^
  --region us-east-1
***********************************  Should show both
tgrp-wnxt-integration-user   ← /health  → ASG instance lifecycle
tgrp-wnxt-user-readiness     ← /readiness → ALB traffic control
*********************************** Verify instances register in both target groups (Watch instances come up)
aws autoscaling describe-auto-scaling-groups ^
  --auto-scaling-group-names WNXT-INT-USER-ASG ^
  --query "AutoScalingGroups[*].Instances[*].{ID:InstanceId,State:LifecycleState,Health:HealthStatus}" ^
  --region us-east-1
*********************************** Check Health TG
aws elbv2 describe-target-health ^
  --target-group-arn arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:us-east-1:604009108246:targetgroup/tgrp-wnxt-integration-user/681a4dc3768c2eee ^
  --region us-east-1
*********************************** Check Readiness TG
aws elbv2 describe-target-health ^
  --target-group-arn arn:aws:elasticloadbalancing:us-east-1:604009108246:targetgroup/tgrp-wnxt-int-user-readiness/f41e3007f3d1d40b ^
  --region us-east-1

@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@ Required Fixes

******************************* What we actually need is:
tgrp-wnxt-int-user-readiness receives user traffic via ALB rule
tgrp-wnxt-integration-user receives health check requests only from ALB
******************************* The Real Answer — Weight=0 Trick (Set tgrp-wnxt-integration-user weight to 0 — ALB sends health checks but no traffic:)
What Weight=0 Does
tgrp-wnxt-int-user-readiness100✅ Receives all traffic✅ ALB checks /readiness
tgrp-wnxt-integration-user0❌ No traffic✅ ALB checks /health

This Solves Everything! ✅

ALB sends health checks to both TGs ✅
tgrp-wnxt-integration-user /health non-200
        ↓
ASG health check type ELB
        ↓
ASG detects unhealthy → replaces instance ✅

tgrp-wnxt-int-user-readiness /readiness 503
        ↓
ALB stops traffic → instance stays alive ✅
ASG ignores /readiness result ✅ (weight=0 TG is health-only)

The Definitive Clean Solution
Use EC2 health check type + weight=0 for health TG:
ASG health check: EC2 → detects OS crashes ✅
ALB weight=0 TG: /health → ALB sends health checks ✅
                           → ASG ignores TG results ✅
ALB weight=100 TG: /readiness → controls traffic ✅
